join Lucretia leftmost
Lucretia: Man, if it wasn’t for the whole eldritch-zombies and split-consciousness thing, having these powers would be awesome.  Feels good not needing to rely on anyone!
join Syn_Lucretia rightmost
Syn_Lucretia: Yeah, yeah, it must be nice not being held hostage in an alternate universe. We get it. Anyways, look at what I found!
Lucretia: Is that cthulhu?
Syn_Lucretia: Well, obviously no, but it kinda looks like him. They call it an “Old One” in the painting. They seem to be worshipped like gods? And look in the corner–
Lucretia: Argus.
Syn_Lucretia: Right, but he’s not mentioned anywhere. And given how nearly everything’s covered up or destroyed, I’m guessing this was stuff he didn’t want anyone to see.
Lucretia: So what does it all mean?
Syn_Lucretia: I’m not sure. But maybe Argus has been causing chaos for longer than we realize.
Lucretia: I’m starting to worry this will be a lot harder than just getting him to undo the deal.
Syn_Lucretia: Depends how badly we care about saving the world.